NeneEngine @PROJECT_VERSION@
====================

A C++20 game engine with a DirectX 12 renderer, an ECS world, Jolt physics
and an editor.

Source code: https://github.com/NeneTech-Ind/NeneEngine


Requirements
------------

- Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit
- A graphics card with DirectX 12 support

No installation is needed: everything the engine uses is in this folder.


Run
---

Start NeneEngine.exe. The editor opens the demo scene in Edit mode.
A stress scene with ten thousand cubes, assets/scenes/stress_scene.json,
can be opened from the File menu.

Each run writes a separate nene_engine-<date>-<time>-<timestamp>-<pid>.log
file in %LOCALAPPDATA%/NeneEngine/logs/.
At startup, the editor keeps the 20 most recent logs. Older logs that are
still open are kept until a later startup.

On the first start Windows may ask whether NeneEngine can use the network.
The engine opens a port only for the Tracy profiler, so access can be denied.

Command line options:

  --smoke-test          Initialize the engine, load the scene and exit
  --wait-for-profiler   Wait up to 30 seconds for a Tracy profiler to connect


Controls
--------

  Right mouse + move     Look around
  W, A, S, D             Move the camera
  Space, Ctrl            Move the camera up, down
  Shift                  Move faster

  Ctrl+P                 Enter or leave Play mode
  Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Y         Undo, redo
  Ctrl+S, Ctrl+Shift+S   Save scene, save scene as
  Ctrl+O                 Load scene
  W, E, R                Move, rotate, scale gizmo
  X                      Switch gizmo between local and world space
  F3                     Show or hide colliders


